window.KG_MESSAGES = {"site.name":"Blood Gas Atlas","site.desc":"Step-by-step blood gas evaluation and learning: acid–base, compensation, anion gap, oxygenation, lactate and DKA.","nav.main":"Main menu","nav.atlas":"← All atlases","nav.lang":"Language","tab.home":"Home","tab.eval":"Evaluate","tab.learn":"Learn","tab.cases":"Cases","tab.formulas":"Formulas","tab.src":"Sources","foot.by":"Prepared by Anesthesia Briefs and Anestezi Rehberi.","foot.note":"An educational tool for blood gas interpretation and clinical reasoning. It does not replace patient assessment.","foot.privacy":"Entered values are calculated only in your browser; they are not sent anywhere and are not stored. Do not enter patient identifiers.","foot.sib":"Sister atlases:","foot.atlas1":"Anesthesia Machine Atlas","foot.atlas2":"Advanced Monitoring Atlas","foot.atlas3":"Mechanical Ventilation Atlas","foot.contact":"Contact","foot.visActive":"currently active","foot.visToday":"Today","foot.visMonth":"This month","status.hesaplandi":"Calculated","status.veri_eksik":"Data missing","status.uygulanamaz":"Not applicable","status.gozden_gecirilmeli":"Review needed","mod.quality":"Sample and data quality","mod.hh":"Internal consistency of values","mod.ph":"pH direction","mod.proc":"Possible processes and compensation","mod.ag":"Anion gap","mod.agc":"Albumin-corrected anion gap","mod.delta":"Delta gap and delta ratio","mod.pf":"PaO₂/FiO₂","mod.aa":"Alveolar–arterial O₂ difference (room air)","mod.cao2":"Arterial oxygen content","mod.dyshb":"Dyshemoglobin context","mod.lactate":"Lactate","mod.dka":"Diabetic ketoacidosis criteria","mod.dkares":"DKA resolution criteria","mod.scope":"Scope","m.age_missing":"No age group selected. Select an age group to display the appropriate calculations and interpretations.","m.sample_cord":"Cord blood is assessed in a separate pathway; standard adult interpretation does not apply.","m.sample_circuit":"A circuit (ECMO/bypass) sample is not a patient arterial sample; this version has no circuit blood gas module.","m.input_errors":"Some inputs cannot be used until corrected (fields with red borders below). The related calculations were performed without these fields or were stopped.","m.sample_unknown":"Sample type unknown. Arterial was not assumed: arterial interpretation and oxygenation calculations were stopped. Select the sample type.","m.sample_venous":"Venous sample: pH and HCO₃ are shown as context; arterial compensation classification, PaO₂/FiO₂, A–a and CaO₂ are turned off. No fixed venous-to-arterial conversion is applied.","m.sample_capillary":"Capillary sample: PO₂ is not used in place of arterial oxygenation; arterial compensation classification is turned off.","m.preg_unknown":"Pregnancy status unknown: the non-pregnant adult reference was used.","m.preg_yes":"Pregnancy present: standard adult disorder classification was stopped.","m.temp_unknown":"Temperature reporting status unknown; make sure that temperature-corrected and uncorrected values are not mixed.","m.temp_mixed":"Temperature-corrected and uncorrected values are mixed: the combined consistency check was not performed and the integrated interpretation was suspended.","m.time_missing":"Sample time not entered. Time is required for serial evaluation and for combining different panels.","m.mixed_times":"Chemistry and blood gas are from different times or samples: no integrated interpretation is made until the justification for combining them is verified.","m.no_critical_alarm":"This site has no approved critical value thresholds; out-of-reference values are not shown as urgent alarms. Follow your institution's critical value reporting rules.","m.hh_consistent":"The entered pH, PCO₂ and actual HCO₃ values are mathematically consistent within the rounding margin of the number of digits entered and the difference between the IFCC constants used by blood gas analyzers (pK 6.095; CO₂ solubility coefficient 0.0307 mmol/L/mmHg) and the atlas formula (pK 6.1; 0.03).","m.hh_inconsistent":"The entered pH, PCO₂ and actual HCO₃ values are not mathematically consistent with each other. Transcription error, HCO₃ type (actual/standard) and sample time should be reviewed. Integrated interpretation is suspended until this is resolved.","m.hh_not_validation":"Consistency does not prove that the sample was taken from the right patient or that the analyzer is working correctly. If the device calculates HCO₃ with this equation, this check is not an independent verification.","m.ph_within_continue":"pH is within the reference range. This does not mean the evaluation is finished: opposing processes can make pH appear normal. Continue with the compensation and anion gap review.","m.ph_not_arterial":"The arterial adult pH reference was not applied to this sample type.","m.ph_preg":"In pregnancy, no label was assigned using the adult reference.","m.proc_sample_unknown":"Arterial compensation calculations were not performed because the sample type is unknown.","m.proc_not_arterial":"Compensation formulas are for arterial samples; no definitive compensation label is assigned for this sample.","m.proc_suspended":"Process and compensation interpretation was suspended because the values are inconsistent or could not be combined.","m.proc_multi":"Each possible process is shown as a separate hypothesis together with its expected response. Finding one does not exclude the others; evaluate together with the clinical history and previous measurements.","m.proc_none":"HCO₃ and PCO₂ are at the starting points of the compensation formulas (24 mmol/L, 40 mmHg). This does not prove the absence of opposing processes; look at the anion gap and the clinical context.","h.met_acid":"Metabolic acidosis hypothesis","h.met_alk":"Metabolic alkalosis hypothesis","h.resp_acid":"Respiratory acidosis hypothesis","h.resp_alk":"Respiratory alkalosis hypothesis","h.why.met_acid":"HCO₃ {h} mmol/L, below the formula starting point of 24.","h.why.met_alk":"HCO₃ {h} mmol/L, above the formula starting point of 24.","h.why.resp_acid":"PCO₂ {p} mmHg, above the formula starting point of 40.","h.why.resp_alk":"PCO₂ {p} mmHg, below the formula starting point of 40.","h.align.same":"Same direction as pH","h.align.opposite":"Opposite to the pH direction (this change may also be a response)","h.align.neutral":"pH within reference: no directional clue","h.met.within":"Measured PaCO₂ {m} mmHg, within the expected range ({lo}–{hi}). Consistent with the expected respiratory response.","h.met.above.met_acid":"Measured PaCO₂ {m} mmHg, above the expected range ({lo}–{hi}): an additional acidifying respiratory effect (respiratory acidosis) is possible.","h.met.below.met_acid":"Measured PaCO₂ {m} mmHg, below the expected range ({lo}–{hi}): an additional alkalinizing respiratory effect (respiratory alkalosis) is possible.","h.met.above.met_alk":"Measured PaCO₂ {m} mmHg, above the expected range ({lo}–{hi}): additional respiratory acidosis is possible.","h.met.below.met_alk":"Measured PaCO₂ {m} mmHg, below the expected range ({lo}–{hi}): additional respiratory alkalosis is possible.","h.resp.est":"Expected HCO₃ for the acute model: {a} · for the chronic model: {c} · measured: {m} mmol/L.","h.resp.equidistant":"The measured value is equally distant from the acute and chronic model estimates. This does not establish the duration of the process; a mixed process is also possible.","h.resp.nearer":"closer to the {near} model","h.resp.between":"The measured value lies between the two estimates; closer to the {near} model. An acute–chronic intermediate state or a mixed process is also possible.","h.resp.below":"The measured value is below both model estimates. These are point estimates and no tolerance is defined; the difference alone is not evidence of an additional metabolic process; evaluate with the clinical context.","h.resp.above":"The measured value is above both model estimates. These are point estimates and no tolerance is defined; the difference alone is not evidence of an additional metabolic process; evaluate with the clinical context.","h.resp.chronicity":"Without knowing the duration and a previous blood gas, no single chronicity label is assigned.","h.near.acute":"akut","h.near.chronic":"kronik","h.near.equal":"equidistant from both models","m.ag_gas_hco3":"Blood gas HCO₃ was used instead of TCO₂ (different method). Do not compare directly with a gap calculated using chemistry TCO₂.","m.ag_negative":"The anion gap is negative. It was not rounded to zero: possible causes including analytical problems, input error and albumin should be reviewed.","m.ag_low_review":"The anion gap is below the local reference: possible causes including an analytical problem, input error and albumin should be reviewed.","m.ag_no_interval":"Because no local AG reference range was entered, no definitive \"high / normal\" label was assigned; no single universal normal value is used.","ag.cls.high":"Above the local reference ({lo}–{hi})","ag.cls.within":"Within the local reference range ({lo}–{hi})","ag.cls.low":"Below the local reference ({lo}–{hi})","ag.vs.above":"Above the entered reference value ({r})","ag.vs.below":"Below the entered reference value ({r})","ag.vs.equal":"Equal to the entered reference value ({r})","m.agc_missing":"No correction was made because albumin or the albumin reference was not entered; the measured gap remains valid.","m.agc_not_lactate":"The correction coefficient is a model. The corrected AG is not reliable enough to exclude hyperlactatemia; measure lactate directly if needed.","m.delta_needs_tco2":"The delta calculation requires chemistry TCO₂; it was not performed with blood gas HCO₃.","m.delta_no_high_ag":"The gap ({ag}) is not above the entered reference value ({r}): since there is no high anion gap acidosis context, the delta was not calculated.","m.delta_pos":"Positive difference: the AG increase is greater than the HCO₃ decrease. An additional metabolic process (in the direction that raises HCO₃) may be present.","m.delta_neg":"Negative difference: the HCO₃ decrease is greater than the AG increase. An additional metabolic process (in the direction that lowers HCO₃ without increasing the gap) may be present.","m.delta_zero_gap":"Difference is zero: the AG increase and the HCO₃ decrease are equal.","m.delta_no_cutoffs":"Thresholds are method-dependent; categorical definitive diagnoses and colored diagnostic bands are not used. Individual baseline values, the type of acid and concurrent processes affect interpretation.","m.delta_uncorrected":"The measured AG was used because albumin correction could not be performed.","m.delta_ratio_closed":"The denominator of the ratio (HCO₃ reference − TCO₂) is zero or negative: the ratio was not calculated.","m.ox_venous":"In a venous sample, PO₂ is not used in place of arterial oxygenation.","m.ox_capillary":"In a capillary sample, PO₂ is not used in place of arterial oxygenation.","m.ox_sample_unknown":"Oxygenation calculations were not performed because the sample type is unknown.","m.fio2_input_error":"The FiO₂ entry needs to be corrected; the value was not changed automatically.","m.pf_approx":"FiO₂ is estimated (or its source is unknown): the result is approximate.","m.pf_not_ards":"The ratio alone is not a diagnosis of ARDS; other conditions such as timing of onset, imaging and the cause of edema are required. This card does not classify adult ARDS.","m.aa_supplemental":"Supplemental oxygen present: in this first version only the room air formula is defined; the A–a difference was not calculated.","m.aa_assumptions":"Assumptions: FiO₂ 0.21; water vapor pressure 47 mmHg (approximately 37 °C); respiratory quotient R = 0.8.","m.cao2_dyshb":"COHb/MetHb elevation or suspicion present: the simplified oxygen content calculation was turned off.","m.cao2_spo2":"SpO₂ is not used in place of arterial saturation (SaO₂).","m.cohb_context":"Carbon monoxide: standard two-wavelength pulse oximetry may not be reliable; COHb is measured by blood co-oximetry. Time elapsed since exposure and oxygen already given affect the result; the COHb percentage alone does not indicate clinical severity.","m.methb_context":"Methemoglobin: a mismatch between saturation and clinical appearance and a history of oxidizing agents should be investigated; MetHb measured by co-oximetry is kept separate.","m.spo2_unreliable":"A normal-appearing PO₂ or SpO₂ does not provide reassurance.","m.lac_single":"Single lactate value: change was not calculated. For serial measurement, add a second value with its time.","m.lac_zero":"The first lactate value is zero: percent change was not calculated.","m.lac_not_clearance":"This is arithmetic change; it is not a measurement of true physiological clearance. A positive value indicates a decrease, a negative value an increase.","m.lac_not_sepsis":"Assess lactate with perfusion findings, sampling time and interventions.","m.dka_not_diagnosis":"Meeting numeric criteria is not equal to a clinical diagnosis. Insulin, potassium or bicarbonate doses are not calculated on this site.","m.dka_euglycemic":"Because of euglycemic presentations, a normal glucose alone does not exclude DKA; a history of diabetes alone satisfies this component.","m.dka_venous_ok":"Venous pH may be used in the DKA criteria; this card is independent of the arterial compensation calculation.","m.dka_sample_unknown":"Sample type unknown; interpret the pH component together with the sample type.","m.dkares_not_ag":"Anion gap closure is not used as a criterion for DKA resolution.","m.dkares_hyperchloremic":"Post-treatment hyperchloremic acidosis can confound HCO₃ interpretation.","m.preg_physiology":"In pregnancy, values differ from those of non-pregnant adults because of increased ventilation. An anesthesia physiology review reports PaCO₂ of approximately 30–32 mmHg, HCO₃ of approximately 20–21 mEq/L and pH 7.42–7.44. These describe healthy pregnancy physiology; they are not universal alarm limits for trimester, disease or laboratory.","err.ambiguous_decimal":"Both a period and a comma are present: clarify the decimal separator.","err.not_number":"The number could not be read.","err.negative":"Negative value is invalid.","err.pco2_zero":"PCO₂ cannot be zero.","err.fio2_fraction_gt1":"In fraction units, FiO₂ cannot be greater than 1. If you typed 40, select percent (%) as the unit; the value is not changed automatically.","err.fio2_percent_gt100":"FiO₂ in percent cannot be greater than 100.","err.fio2_zero":"FiO₂ cannot be zero.","err.sat_percent_gt100":"Saturation in percent cannot be greater than 100.","err.sat_fraction_gt1":"In fraction units, saturation cannot be greater than 1.","mod.age":"Age arithmetic","mod.oi":"Oxygenation index (OI)","mod.osi":"Oxygen saturation index (OSI)","mod.pards":"PARDS oxygenation criterion (PALICC-2)","mod.nards":"NARDS oxygenation severity (Montreux)","mod.rds":"European RDS consensus profile","mod.hcap":"Hypercapnia context (adult education card)","m.hc_open_note":"This card opened because PCO₂ is above the starting point of the compensation formulas (40 mmHg). 40 mmHg is not a hypercapnia, NIV or treatment threshold.","m.hc_etiology_open":"Etiology open: COPD is not diagnosed from a blood gas (the diagnosis is confirmed by post-bronchodilator spirometry). Causes such as obesity hypoventilation, sleep disorders, neuromuscular and drug-induced hypoventilation are considered separately.","m.hc_copd_user":"COPD diagnosis was entered by the user as confirmed. Even so, the blood gas alone does not show the cause of the CO₂ elevation in this sample.","m.hc_venous":"Venous sample: PCO₂ is not labelled as PaCO₂ and arterial thresholds are not applied to the venous result. Venous pH/HCO₃ may be useful in the initial assessment; venous PO₂ does not indicate oxygenation.","m.hc_sample_other":"Sample type is not arterial or is unknown: acute/chronic interpretation and arterial thresholds were not applied. First verify the sample type.","m.hc_no_arterial_frame":"Acute/chronic hypotheses and pH context are shown only for arterial samples.","m.hc_no_baseline":"No previous stable gas entered: the distinction between acute, chronic or acute-on-chronic cannot be established from a single gas; the statements below are possibilities only.","m.hc_vs_baseline":"The difference from the entered previous stable arterial gas is shown. The difference alone does not prove the time of onset or the cause; it is read together with the clinical course.","m.hc_baseline_limited":"A previous gas was entered but it was not confirmed to be arterial or taken during a stable period: the difference is only a numeric comparison and is not accepted as a baseline value.","m.hc_acute_possible":"Measured HCO₃ is closer to the acute buffering expectation: may be consistent with an acute process. This is not a test that measures disease duration.","m.hc_chronic_possible":"Measured HCO₃ is close to or above the chronic renal adaptation expectation: may be consistent with chronic adaptation; an additional metabolic process has not been excluded. No \"definitely chronic\" label is assigned.","m.hc_hco3_above":"HCO₃ is above even the chronic expectation: the possibility of additional metabolic alkalosis (diuretic, vomiting, alkali, posthypercapnic state) is evaluated in context.","m.hc_hco3_below":"HCO₃ is below even the acute expectation: metabolic acidosis may accompany the respiratory component; the chronicity coefficient alone does not explain this picture.","m.hc_coef_note":"On this site the chronic expectation is calculated with a coefficient of 0.35 mmol/L/mmHg. In a study of 28 stable patients (PaCO₂ approximately 44–69 mmHg) the slope was approximately 0.48; this result cannot be generalized to severe hypercapnia or mixed disorders and was not made the default.","m.hc_suspended":"Acid–base interpretation suspended (HH inconsistency or mixed temperature reporting): acute/chronic and pH context were not shown.","m.hc_metab_ctx_present":"Kidney, diuretic, alkali or vomiting context entered: the HCO₃ change is not explained by renal compensation alone; the metabolic process is evaluated separately.","m.hc_metab_ctx_unknown":"Part of the kidney function, diuretic, alkali or vomiting context is unknown: compensation interpretation is therefore limited.","m.hc_acidemia":"Respiratory acidemia: assess work of breathing, respiratory rate, consciousness and hemodynamics. ERS/ATS and BTS/ICS criteria for starting NIV are explained in separate lesson tables.","m.hc_normal_ph":"pH is within the adult education range but PCO₂ is high: a normal pH does not mean a safe patient or a normal gas; the possibility of chronic adaptation or a mixed process is evaluated in context.","m.hc_spo2_separate":"Saturation or oxygen support entered: SpO₂ does not measure CO₂. Oxygenation and ventilation are evaluated separately; a normal SpO₂ is not an indicator of adequate ventilation.","m.hc_acute_not_longterm":"Gas taken in the acute phase: the question of long-term (home) NIV or home oxygen is evaluated separately and in the stable phase; eligibility is not inferred from this gas.","m.hc_no_treatment":"This card does not produce treatment, oxygen target selection, ventilator settings, medication or repeat sampling time.","m.hc_scope_ped":"The COPD/hypercapnia card is for adults only; adult COPD thresholds are not carried over to children and neonates.","m.hc_scope_preg":"The COPD/hypercapnia card is not applied in the context of pregnancy, labor and postpartum; the pregnancy modules work with their own sources.","m.hc_not_open":"Hypercapnia context was entered but PCO₂ is not above the formula's starting point (40 mmHg): the card was not opened.","m.hc_need_pco2":"PCO₂ is required for the hypercapnia context.","mod.hie":"Encephalopathy (HIE) warning","mod.delivery":"Delivery room SpO₂ target","mod.cord":"Cord blood sample","mod.cordpair":"Cord artery–vein pair","mod.base":"Base excess / base deficit","m.scope_pediatric":"Child: the adult automatic interpretation (compensation, albumin/delta, A–a, CaO₂, adult DKA) is not used. Only the modules supported in the second round are open; there is no universal pediatric normal value.","m.scope_neonatal":"Neonate: the adult automatic interpretation is not used. Automatic compensation and mixed-disorder classification have not been enabled for neonates; only supported calculations are shown.","m.cap_perfusion":"Capillary sample and impaired peripheral perfusion: reliability may be reduced. If the result does not match the clinical picture, resampling is considered.","m.cap_15min":"The capillary sample appears to have been analyzed later than 15 minutes; AARC recommends analyzing capillary samples within 15 minutes.","m.neo_no_ga":"Gestational age at birth was not entered: no adult threshold is assigned to the neonate; the age-specific interpretation context is missing.","m.no_bicarb_dose":"This site does not calculate a bicarbonate dose for low HCO₃ or base deficit.","m.ph_local_ref":"The label is based on the local reference range entered (it should be specific to age, sample type and analyzer). Study references are not automatically assigned in place of the local range.","m.ref_source_missing":"The source of the local reference (age group, sample type, analyzer, year) was not entered; verify the label with this information.","m.ph_ref_needed":"No local, age- and sample-specific reference was entered for this age group: no \"normal\" or \"abnormal\" label was given. The value is shown as an observation only.","m.proc_ped":"Adult compensation formulas are not an automatic diagnosis validated at every age; process classification for children and neonates is disabled in this version. Henderson–Hasselbalch and AG arithmetic are shown for explanation.","m.ped_not_validated":"This calculation was defined for adults in the first round; it is disabled for children and neonates in this version.","m.lac_ped":"The pediatric Surviving Sepsis Campaign 2026 presents lactate measurement at initial evaluation in possible sepsis as a strong recommendation; certainty of evidence is very low. Healthy cohort values from the first minutes after birth are not used as a pediatric threshold.","m.dka_neonatal":"There is no DKA profile for neonates in this package.","m.dkares_ped":"Adult DKA resolution thresholds are not copied to children; no decision to stop treatment is produced.","m.uk_scale_adult":"The adult criterion defines urine ketones on the + scale (≥2+); the small/moderate/large scale was not mapped, so this sub-criterion was treated as missing data.","m.uk_scale_ped":"The ISPAD criterion defines urine ketones as moderate/large; the + scale was not mapped, so this sub-criterion was treated as missing data.","m.dka_ped_profile":"Profile: ISPAD 2022 pediatric DKA. Glucose >11 mmol/L, venous pH <7.3 or serum HCO₃ <18 mmol/L, and β-hydroxybutyrate ≥3 mmol/L or moderate/large urine ketones are evaluated together.","m.dka_ketone_missing":"Ketone data missing: the criterion was shown as \"no data\", not counted as negative.","m.dka_glucose_conv":"The ISPAD threshold is defined in mmol/L; the mg/dL value was compared after dividing by 18.016 (glucose molar mass 180.16 g/mol).","m.dka_ped_venous_ph":"The ISPAD acidosis criterion is defined by venous pH; this sample is not venous.","m.dka_ped_euglycemic":"Acidosis and ketosis criteria were met although glucose is below the threshold: clinical review including euglycemic DKA is needed; glucose does not exclude a suspected case.","m.dka_sev_mismatch":"pH and HCO₃ indicate different severities: both were shown, the more severe one was not hidden.","m.dka_sev_not_dx":"The severity table alone is not a DKA diagnosis. No insulin, fluid or bicarbonate dose is produced.","m.dka_neuro_urgent":"Neurological deterioration: not considered safe even if glucose improves. Time-sensitive urgent clinical evaluation for cerebral injury is needed.","m.base_known":"The BE/BD value is shown with the selected algorithm and its sign. Blood and extracellular fluid (ECF) algorithms are not the same.","m.base_unknown":"BE/BD algorithm unknown: threshold classification and sign conversion were stopped. Conversion between different algorithms cannot be done by only changing the sign.","m.base_no_threshold":"This site does not perform threshold classification for BE/BD; the value alone does not give the cause of acidosis. pH, PCO₂ and clinical context remain visible.","m.age_not_threshold":"Postmenstrual age is a calendar calculation, not a clinical threshold. A preterm infant is not moved to the child or adult engine based only on chronological day count.","m.oi_not_arterial":"OI and PaO₂/FiO₂ are calculated only with arterial PO₂; they were not produced for this sample.","m.oi_paw_not_map":"OI requires mean AIRWAY pressure (cmH₂O); it is not filled with mean arterial pressure.","m.oi_index_not_dx":"It is an index, not a diagnosis on its own. A high index may mean lower oxygenation with more support.","m.oi_not_concurrent":"Support values are not concurrent with the blood gas: the values were combined but not accepted as concurrent.","m.oi_concurrent_check":"Verify that FiO₂ and mean airway pressure are the values at the time of sampling.","m.site_mismatch":"Preductal SpO₂ was combined with postductal (umbilical artery) PaO₂: the measurement sites may not represent the same oxygenation.","m.osi_palicc_only":"OSI falls under PALICC-2; it does not replace the Montreux NARDS table.","m.osi_spo2_range":"SpO₂ outside 88–97%: PALICC-2 OSI classification was stopped (arithmetic is shown).","m.osi_signal":"Signal quality was not marked as good and the measurement as stable: OSI classification was stopped.","m.oi_preferred":"OI with arterial PO₂ is available: OI is preferred in the evaluation; OSI is not silently used in its place.","m.pards_need_vent":"Ventilation type was not selected; the PALICC-2 invasive ventilation criterion applies only to invasive ventilation.","m.pards_imv_only":"Only the PALICC-2 OI/OSI thresholds for invasive ventilation are defined in this package; no classification was made for this support type.","m.pards_crit_met":"Oxygenation criterion met numerically (OI ≥4 or OSI ≥5).","m.pards_crit_not_met":"Oxygenation criterion not met. This does not mean \"lung normal\".","m.pards_crit_missing":"No OI or classifiable OSI: the oxygenation criterion could not be evaluated.","m.pards_not_dx":"The oxygenation criterion alone is not a PARDS diagnosis; timing, imaging and etiology are evaluated clinically.","m.pards_not_confirmed":"Clinical PARDS diagnosis not confirmed: only the calculation was shown, no severity label was given.","m.pards_wait_4h":"4 hours have not passed since diagnosis or the duration was not entered: the PALICC-2 severity label was withheld.","m.pards_special_group":"Cyanotic congenital heart disease or invasive ventilation since onset: the standard PARDS severity label is not applied.","m.nards_oi_only":"Montreux oxygenation severity is defined only by OI; PALICC-2 OSI thresholds are not added to this table.","m.nards_not_confirmed":"NARDS context (including exclusion of primary RDS, transient tachypnea and congenital anomalies) was not confirmed: Montreux severity was not given. Not every preterm infant with low oxygenation has NARDS.","m.nards_below":"OI below 4: does not fall within the Montreux oxygenation severity range.","m.nards_table":"Montreux table: 4 ≤ OI < 8 mild · 8 ≤ OI < 16 moderate · OI ≥ 16 severe.","m.rds_target":"European RDS consensus for infants born at <28 weeks receiving oxygen: SpO₂ target 90–94%, alarm limits 89% and 95% (treatment target).","m.rds_weaning":"It states that moderate hypercapnia may be permitted during weaning from ventilation while maintaining pH >7.22.","m.rds_not_normal":"These are not the physiological normal range for all neonates; profile selection does not change ventilator or oxygen settings.","m.hie_expert":"Neurological impairment or perinatal event: time-sensitive neonatologist evaluation is needed. HIE cannot be diagnosed from a blood gas number alone.","m.hie_no_cooling":"This site does not produce therapeutic hypothermia eligibility or a decision to start it.","m.hie_ga36":"AAP 2026 supports the benefit of hypothermia started within the first 6 hours in infants born at ≥36 weeks with moderate–severe HIE; eligibility is determined by clinical evaluation.","m.hie_ga35":"For 35 weeks 0 days–35 weeks 6 days, AAP states limited evidence and individual risk–benefit assessment; there is no automatic eligibility.","m.hie_ga33":"In a randomized trial of infants at 33–35 weeks, hypothermia showed no benefit for death/disability; term evidence is not generalized to this group.","m.hie_ga_lt33":"Hypothermia evidence for below 33 weeks is not summarized in this package.","m.hie_ga_unknown":"Gestational age unknown; the group covered by the evidence could not be determined.","m.delivery_minute_needed":"Minute after birth unknown: the minute-specific SpO₂ target was not shown.","m.delivery_target":"Preductal SpO₂ target in the AHA 2025 algorithm (delivery room, completed minute).","m.delivery_no_row":"The algorithm table has no row for this minute (the table includes minutes 2, 3, 4, 5 and 10); no target is produced for intermediate minutes.","m.delivery_room_only":"These are delivery room targets; they are not carried over to later intensive care days. Evaluation is done together with ventilation, heart rate and clinical condition.","m.delivery_preductal":"The targets are for preductal measurement (right hand or right wrist); the oximeter site was not selected as preductal.","m.cord_separate":"Cord blood is a separate record type: it is not interpreted the same as the infant's blood gas hours later; the adult and pediatric engines were not run.","m.cord_vessel_unknown":"Vessel uncertain: no interpretation is made as if there were an arterial result.","m.cord_no_arterial":"No arterial interpretation is made for a single sample from an uncertain vessel.","m.cord_single":"Single sample: artery and vein should be recorded together with separate identities; birth, clamping, sampling and analysis times are kept.","m.cord_no_asphyxia":"This site does not produce \"birth asphyxia certain\", \"injury certain\" or liability output.","m.cord_ph_not_prognosis":"Low cord pH is associated with adverse outcomes; on its own it does not determine individual neurological prognosis or the cause of the event.","m.cord_pair_needed":"Enter the artery and vein values separately for the pair quality review.","m.cord_pair_suspect":"ΔpH <0.02 or ΔPCO₂ <0.5 kPa: the two samples may have been taken from the same vessel (historical quality criterion). This is not a definitive vessel identification test.","m.cord_pair_no_flag":"The difference is not below the warning limit of this quality rule.","m.cord_no_relabel":"Samples are not automatically relabeled.","m.cord_not_proof":"The absence of a warning does not prove that the samples were definitely taken from the correct vessels.","m.cord_pair_partial":"Only one parameter of the pair was entered; the other difference was not evaluated.","err.spo2_fraction_like":"SpO₂ is entered as a percentage (for example 95). For a value like 0.95, verify the unit; the value is not converted automatically.","err.ga_decimal":"Gestational week must be a whole number; enter the day in the separate field (30.4 weeks is not accepted).","err.ga_days_range":"Gestational day must be a whole number between 0 and 6.","err.not_integer":"Must be a whole number.","err.analysis_before_sample":"Analysis time cannot be before sampling time.","err.sample_before_birth":"Sampling time cannot be before birth time.","err.fio2_unit_missing":"The FiO₂ unit (fraction or percentage) must be selected explicitly; it is not guessed.","mod.preg":"Pregnancy physiology","mod.co2rel":"Relative CO₂ rise","mod.o2target":"Oxygen target profile","mod.fetal":"Mother–fetus distinction","mod.pe":"Suspected pulmonary embolism","mod.o2delivery":"Oxygen pressure and oxygen delivery","mod.sepsis":"Maternal sepsis context","m.sample_fetal":"Fetal sample: maternal thresholds are not applied; there is no automatic interpretation for fetal scalp samples in this version. Fetal pH is not calculated from maternal pH.","m.teen_preg":"Adolescent pregnancy: the pediatric profile is kept, pregnancy thresholds are not carried over to the child; age-specific evaluation and the obstetric team are needed.","m.ctx_labor":"Context: labor. The stage of labor and pushing may affect lactate and respiration; serial measurement and clinical condition are evaluated together.","m.ctx_postpartum":"Postpartum: there is no automatic switch to the non-pregnant adult reference; there is no single validated time to return to normal for all parameters. Evaluation for sepsis and thromboembolism continues.","m.ctx_breastfeeding":"Context: breastfeeding. In unexplained acidosis and ketones, lactation ketoacidosis becomes visible in the differential diagnosis; breastfeeding alone does not establish a diagnosis.","m.ctx_breastfeeding_note":"In a breastfeeding person, low energy/carbohydrate intake and additional stress are the context of the rare lactation ketoacidosis; the evidence is based on case reports.","m.owner_unknown":"Whom the sample belongs to (mother, fetus, cord) was not selected; verify the sample owner for maternal interpretation.","m.altitude_unknown":"Altitude was not entered; unknown altitude is not counted as zero. Pregnancy review ranges are affected by altitude.","m.proc_preg":"Standard adult process and compensation classification is not performed in pregnancy: there is no validated per-trimester pregnancy compensation formula, and physiological adaptation is not labeled as a pathological process.","m.proc_postpartum":"Postpartum: there is no automatic switch to standard adult process classification; the time to return to normal is not validated.","m.lac_labor":"During labor, especially with pushing, lactate may rise. This alone is not a diagnosis of sepsis; however, the clinical deterioration warning is not dismissed by attributing the rise to labor alone.","m.lac_lt4_not_exclude":"Lactate below 4 mmol/L does not exclude sepsis.","m.lac_preg_cohort":"In a selected labor cohort (n=1279), median lactate 1.8 mmol/L, ≥2 mmol/L 40.8%, ≥4 mmol/L 4.7% were reported. This is a cohort observation; it is not a normal range or an alarm limit.","m.preg_dka_no_glucose_gate":"In pregnancy DKA may develop with lower glucose and rapidly: glucose is not an exclusion gate. Ketones, pH, HCO₃, AG, diabetes/insulin history and clinical condition are shown together; the thresholds are from the adult consensus, there is no validated pregnancy-specific threshold.","m.preg_ketone_assess":"If a pregnant person with diabetes is hyperglycemic or feels unwell, urgent ketone assessment is recommended.","m.preg_euglycemic":"Glucose is not high, but there are ketone or acidosis findings or ketones are unknown: euglycemic DKA is not considered excluded; clinical evaluation is needed.","m.ketosis_not_ketoacidosis":"Ketones present but no acidosis criterion: asymptomatic ketosis and ketoacidosis are not the same; it is not called definite ketoacidosis.","m.dka_euglycemic_diff":"Differential evaluation: diabetic ketoacidosis, including euglycemic DKA.","m.starvation_diff":"Differential evaluation: starvation ketoacidosis with reduced intake or vomiting; new diabetes, infection and other high-gap causes are not considered excluded.","m.vomiting_alkalosis":"Vomiting can also lead to metabolic alkalosis; the acid–base picture is evaluated together with chloride, ketones and fluid loss.","m.lactation_diff":"Differential evaluation: lactation ketoacidosis in a breastfeeding person (rare; based on case reports).","m.trigger_noted":"Marked as a trigger: insulin pump problem or steroid exposure.","m.preg_physiology_review":"In pregnancy, increased ventilation lowers PaCO₂, and renal bicarbonate excretion increases. The ranges from reviews are shown side by side below with their sources; they are not merged and are not used as a laboratory normal.","m.preg_not_healthy":"The statement \"may be consistent with pregnancy physiology\" does not mean \"healthy\" or \"no disease\"; the previous result, clinical condition, ketones and lactate are evaluated separately.","m.preg_ranges_arterial_only":"The review ranges are for arterial samples; they were not transferred to this sample.","m.preg_low_hco3":"In pregnancy, low HCO₃ alone does not mean new metabolic acidosis.","m.preg_rel_co2":"A PaCO₂ of 35–40 mmHg, which may fall within the usual range outside pregnancy, may suggest a relative CO₂ rise and ventilatory deterioration in a symptomatic pregnant person. This range alone is not a diagnosis of respiratory failure.","m.no_intubation_order":"The site does not recommend intubation or ventilator settings; work of breathing and trend are evaluated clinically.","m.o2_no_profile":"Oxygen target profile not selected: the different targets in the sources are not averaged and no single default target is produced. Specify the profile chosen by the institution or specialist.","m.o2_hypercapnia_expert":"Risk of hypercapnic respiratory failure: the general target is not silently applied; specialist and blood gas evaluation is needed.","m.o2_bts_hypercapnic":"BTS 2017, SpO₂ 88–92% when at risk of hypercapnic respiratory failure (special context; not applied to all pregnant patients).","m.o2_bts_general":"BTS 2017, SpO₂ 94–98% for most acutely ill pregnant patients (pregnancy recommendations grade D; exceptions are set by the institution).","m.o2_bts_hc_unknown":"BTS profile selected but hypercapnia risk unknown: neither the general nor the hypercapnic target was selected.","m.o2_user_profile":"The target entered by the institution or specialist is shown.","m.o2_user_profile_missing":"Institution or specialist profile selected; enter the target range.","m.o2_no_vent_order":"No ventilator setting or permissive hypercapnia order is produced to bring PaCO₂ to a number.","m.maternal_not_fetal":"Good maternal oxygenation does not show that the fetus is definitely well; fetal status requires clinical obstetric evaluation.","m.no_fetal_ph":"Fetal pH is not calculated from maternal pH.","m.fetal_no_routine_o2":"Routine maternal oxygen is not recommended for category II/III fetal heart rate tracings without maternal hypoxia (ACOG No. 10, 2025; NICE NG229). Obstetric assessment is required.","m.pe_not_excluded":"Normal PaO₂/SpO₂ or low PCO₂ does not exclude pulmonary embolism; blood gas cannot replace the clinical diagnostic pathway in pregnancy.","m.o2_delivery_not_pao2":"PaO₂ and oxygen content are not the same: a normal PaO₂ does not exclude the effect of severe anemia or hemorrhage on oxygen delivery. Oxygen delivery also depends on circulation.","m.no_transfusion_order":"Blood loss, transfusion dose or cause of shock is not calculated from a single lactate or BE.","m.sepsis_consider_smfm":"Consider sepsis when suspected or confirmed infection is accompanied by otherwise unexplained organ dysfunction, even without fever (SMFM 2023, reaffirmed in 2025).","m.nice_branch_met":"In the NICE NG255 high-risk context, lactate >4 mmol/L or systolic pressure ≤90 mmHg affects the evaluation for escalation of care. This is not a sepsis diagnosis.","m.nice_branch_not_met":"The NICE high-risk criterion of lactate >4 mmol/L or systolic blood pressure ≤90 mmHg was not met. This does not mean low risk; this site does not provide the full NICE risk assessment.","m.nice_branch_missing":"Lactate or systolic pressure missing for the NICE branch.","m.nice_needs_context":"Clinical high-risk and suspected-infection context not selected: the lactate and pressure thresholds are not used as the full NICE sepsis algorithm.","m.sepsis_no_exclusion":"Normal lactate or absence of fever does not automatically exclude sepsis.","m.no_fluid_order":"The site does not produce fluid bolus, antibiotic or delivery decisions.","err.pao2_zero":"PO₂ cannot be zero; OI and P/F are not calculated with this value.","err.paw_zero":"Mean airway pressure was entered as zero; OI/OSI were not calculated. Verify the value.","err.range_reversed":"The lower value of the range is greater than the upper value; the range was not used. Correct the values.","err.pnd_conflict":"The postnatal day calculated from birth and sampling time does not match the manually entered day; age was not calculated.","m.pnd_conflict":"Birth/sampling time conflicts with the manually entered postnatal day: postmenstrual age was not calculated.","m.calc_not_finite":"The calculation did not yield a finite number (invalid denominator); the result and the classification derived from it were not shown.","m.index_unstable":"Measurement marked as not stable: the index is shown but not used for classification.","m.index_validity_unverified":"It was not confirmed that support values are concurrent with the sample and that the measurement is stable: the index is shown but not used for classification.","m.oi_invalid_osi_separate":"OI is not suitable for classification; OSI is evaluated separately if it meets its own conditions.","m.osi_used_oi_invalid":"Because OI is not suitable for classification, OSI meeting its conditions was used.","m.pards_crit_unverified":"The index was calculated but the oxygenation criterion was not evaluated because measurement validity was not confirmed.","m.pards_index_invalid":"No OI or OSI suitable for classification: no severity label was given.","m.pards_special_unknown":"Cyanotic heart disease or invasive ventilation since onset status unknown: the validity of standard severity was not confirmed, no label was given.","m.nards_index_invalid":"OI is not suitable for classification (concurrency or stability not confirmed): Montreux severity was not given.","m.preg_ket_below_dka":"Ketones were measured but are below the selected DKA ketone criterion (β-hydroxybutyrate ≥3 mmol/L or urine ≥2+/moderate-large). This does not mean \"no ketosis\"; conditions such as starvation and lactation ketoacidosis are not excluded by this criterion.","m.preg_acidosis_review":"Acidosis in pregnancy: clinical evaluation is needed regardless of the ketone result; the cause is investigated with differential diagnosis.","m.preg_dka_urgent":"Acidosis with ketones or a history of fasting/vomiting requires urgent assessment in a setting that provides both medical and obstetric care.","m.preg_co2_above":"PaCO₂ is above 40 mmHg in pregnancy and may exceed the level expected in healthy pregnancy. This does not necessarily exceed the nonpregnant adult reference range. Promptly assess work of breathing, measurement trends and clinical condition; a single value does not diagnose respiratory failure.","m.lac_resorted":"Values were sorted by timestamp; the change was calculated between the chronologically first and last measurements.","m.lac_time_tie":"There is more than one value with the same timestamp: temporal change was not calculated.","m.lac_entry_order":"Time information missing or inconsistent: the change is only a comparison by entry order, not a temporal trend.","m.lac_latest_entry":"Lactate times could not be verified chronologically; the last entered value was used.","m.assume_not_pregnant":"Pregnancy context unknown: this classification was shown assuming a non-pregnant adult. If pregnant, in labor or postpartum, select the context; if not, select \"Not pregnant / not applicable\".","err.hco3_zero":"Actual HCO₃ cannot be zero; the Henderson–Hasselbalch calculation (log10) is undefined with this value.","m.age_time_invalid":"Sampling time is before birth time: postnatal age, minutes and postmenstrual age were not calculated from the date. Correct the times.","m.cao2_dyshb_conflict":"COHb/MetHb was measured but \"no dyshemoglobin\" was selected: this conflict is not resolved by confirmation; standard CaO₂ was not calculated.","m.cao2_measured_policy":"This version does not display the standard CaO₂ calculation when COHb or MetHb has been measured. Functional saturation is O₂Hb/(O₂Hb + HHb), whereas fractional O₂Hb is O₂Hb/total Hb; they are not equivalent in the presence of dyshemoglobins. CaO₂ also includes the hemoglobin oxygen-binding coefficient and oxygen dissolved in plasma. This version has no separate calculation pathway for fractional O₂Hb.","mod.sample":"Specimen and measurement quality","m.q_three_lists":"Known error, possible effect and missing quality information are shown separately. Calculations are not stopped; a note is added to cards that may be affected. The accept/reject decision belongs to the institutional protocol.","m.q_no_score":"This site has no specimen reliability score, automatic rejection or artifact correction formula; the sources do not provide a validated score.","qw.q_bubble":"Air bubble seen: PO₂ may be affected in either direction (rise if initially low, fall if high), as may PCO₂, pH and saturation. Removing the bubble does not undo prior gas exchange; a corrected PaO₂ cannot be calculated.","qw.q_heparin_liquid":"Liquid heparin: PCO₂, HCO₃, sodium and other electrolytes (including ionized calcium) may be affected by dilution and cation binding. Dilution cannot be back-calculated from the result; the product's permitted fill range is the reference.","qw.q_clot":"Clot seen: tHb and calculations derived from it, as well as sensor function, may be affected. Removing the clot does not \"rescue\" the sample; the institution's rejection/resampling procedure is applied.","qw.q_hemolysis":"Hemolysis positive: potassium may be falsely high and may mask a true low value. Hemolysis does not exclude a true and urgent potassium disorder; there is no fixed correction.","qw.q_hemolysis_unknown_k":"Hemolysis not measured or the device's capability for this is unknown: the absence of a warning does not mean \"no hemolysis\". Potassium is evaluated together with the clinical picture and the ECG.","qw.q_flush_glucose":"Glucose-containing flush solution in a catheter-drawn sample: risk of falsely high glucose and consequently inappropriate insulin. 0.9% NaCl is recommended for arterial line flushing; a suspect result cannot be made reliable by a dilution correction.","qw.q_flush_unknown":"Sample drawn from a catheter but the flush solution is unknown: glucose contamination cannot be excluded; verify the flush solution, sampling port and infusions.","qw.q_delay_protocol":"Analysis delay exceeds the protocol time entered by the institution. No automatic rejection is made; evaluate according to the institutional protocol. The effect varies by parameter and condition (PO₂ in either direction).","qw.q_transport":"Pneumatic tube transport not validated with this syringe and analyzer, or validation unknown: transport suitability is unknown. Sources report differing results.","qw.q_hydroxo":"Hydroxocobalamin: co-oximetry results (saturation, COHb, MetHb) may be affected on certain analyzer models. Reports are specific to model and software; they do not generalize to all devices.","qw.q_leuko":"Marked leukocytosis: ongoing oxygen consumption in the sample may cause pseudohypoxemia (case-level evidence). True respiratory impairment is not excluded; there is no leukocyte threshold.","qw.q_tco2_hco3":"Chemistry TCO₂ and the HCO₃ calculated on the blood gas are not the same data field. If they differ, check sample time, unit, report field and calculation source; measurement interference is also possible. There is no universal difference threshold, and a difference alone does not indicate high anion gap acidosis.","qw.q_device_error":"Device error code or result outside the measurement range: this is not the same as a true clinical extreme value. Other valid measurements are not deleted.","qw.q_manual":"Values were transcribed manually: verify that the value, unit and field match the report.","m.aff_q_bubble":"Sample note: an air bubble may affect this result (value not corrected).","m.aff_q_heparin_liquid":"Sample note: liquid heparin may affect this result (value not corrected).","m.aff_q_clot":"Sample note: a clot may affect this result.","m.aff_q_flush_glucose":"Sample note: a glucose-containing flush solution may show falsely high glucose.","m.aff_q_flush_unknown":"Sample note: catheter flush solution unknown; glucose contamination cannot be excluded.","m.aff_q_delay_protocol":"Sample note: analysis delay exceeds the institutional protocol.","m.aff_q_transport":"Sample note: transport suitability unknown.","m.aff_q_hydroxo":"Sample note: hydroxocobalamin may affect co-oximetry results (model-specific).","m.aff_q_leuko":"Sample note: in marked leukocytosis PO₂ may be falsely low; true hypoxemia is not excluded.","m.aff_q_tco2_hco3":"Sample note: TCO₂ and calculated HCO₃ are different data fields.","m.aff_q_hemolysis":"Sample note: hemolysis.","m.aff_q_device_error":"Sample note: device error code or result outside the measurement range.","m.aff_q_manual":"Sample note: manual transcription.","m.aff_q_hemolysis_unknown_k":"Sample note: hemolysis status unknown.","tab.serial":"Serial","m.rds_hypocapnia_unverified":"PCO₂ is below 35 mmHg. The European RDS consensus recommendation to avoid hypocapnia (PCO₂ <35 mmHg) applies to the context of confirmed RDS and invasive ventilation; because this context was not entered, the recommendation was not applied to this measurement. Enter the clinical RDS diagnosis and the ventilation type.","m.rds_hypocapnia":"PCO₂ is below 35 mmHg in this measurement: the European RDS consensus recommends avoiding PCO₂ <35 mmHg during ventilation. This recommendation is specific to this profile; it is not a single target for all neonates.","sf.same_time":"Samples with the same time: rate not calculated.","sn.co2_fall_not_success":"PCO₂ has fallen. Assess the response alongside work of breathing, consciousness and hemodynamics; clinical deterioration requires urgent reassessment despite gas improvement.","sn.posthypercapnic_context":"Chronic hypercapnia is confirmed. PCO₂ has fallen, HCO₃ has not decreased and alkalemia has developed. Review prior gases, diuretics, chloride/potassium and kidney function for post-hypercapnic or additional metabolic alkalosis.","sn.co2_fall_alkalemia_general":"PCO₂ has fallen, pH has risen, HCO₃ has not decreased and alkalemia has developed. Check for prior chronic hypercapnia when considering post-hypercapnic alkalosis.","sn.acidbase_matrix_not_equivalent":"Sample type changed or is unknown: acid–base measurements are not directly equivalent. The raw difference is shown; no component or specific serial interpretation was made.","sf.point_validity":"At least one point in this interval has an acid–base validity problem (Henderson–Hasselbalch inconsistency, mixed temperature reporting, or pH/PCO₂/HCO₃ input error). No component-based note was generated.","sf.point_input_errors":"One point in this interval has an input error in a non-acid–base field; the related calculation is disabled, and the acid–base notes were not affected by it.","sf.assume_not_pregnant":"The adult note in this interval relies on a point whose pregnancy context is unknown: it was generated under the assumption of a non-pregnant adult.","sf.hh_suspended":"Acid–base interpretation is suspended in this interval: the difference is raw arithmetic only.","si.unverified":"Identity not verified: no anonymous episode label was entered for the points. The series is built on the assumption that the points come from the same person and the same episode; the site cannot verify this.","si.partial":"Some points lack an anonymous episode label: it could not be verified that all measurements belong to the same person and episode.","si.labels_match":"All points have the same anonymous episode label (input-based matching; this is not clinical identity verification).","si.mismatch":"Episode labels do not match.","sw.duplicate_id":"Duplicate point ID found: the IDs were disambiguated (e.g. N2·2). Check the IDs.","sv.hh_inconsistent":"pH, PCO₂ and HCO₃ are inconsistent with Henderson–Hasselbalch (acid–base interpretation suspended)","sv.temp_mixed":"temperature reporting is mixed (acid–base interpretation suspended)","sv.input_errors":"there is an input error in a non-acid–base field","sv.acidbase_input_error":"there is an error in the pH, PCO₂ or HCO₃ input (acid–base interpretation disabled)","sf.matrix_changed":"Sample type changed: the parameters are not the same measurement.","sf.method_changed":"Device/method changed: the difference is not read as biological change; there is no universal correction factor.","sf.support_changed":"Support (FiO₂/PEEP/mean airway pressure/support type) changed: the value is read together with the support.","sf.value_missing_or_invalid":"Value missing or invalid: no comparison was made (not treated as zero).","sf.not_arterial_both":"At least one sample is nonarterial or its type is unknown: oxygenation was not compared.","sf.albumin_not_concurrent":"Albumin not verified as concurrent with the sample: no corrected AG trend given.","sf.index_not_classifiable":"At least one point is not eligible for OI/OSI classification (concurrency/stability not verified): arithmetic only; no change in severity is inferred.","sf.sample_quality":"There is a sample quality warning for this parameter (value not corrected).","sf.pct_undefined_zero":"Previous value is zero: percent change is undefined.","sn.ph_up_by_co2":"The pH rise accompanies a PCO₂ fall; HCO₃ has not increased. Track the metabolic component separately using HCO₃ and relevant markers.","sn.ph_up_components":"pH has risen. Examine the direction and size of both PCO₂ and HCO₃ changes to explain it.","sn.lactate_fall":"Lactate concentration has decreased. Compare the trend with perfusion findings and support needs; the calculated percentage is not a measurement of physiological clearance.","sn.dka_params_separate":"Glucose, ketones and AG may change at different rates. Assess DKA resolution using ketones and pH/HCO₃; adult criteria appear in each point’s own card.","sn.chloride_rise_context":"Chloride has risen. If HCO₃ stays low as ketones fall, assess a hyperchloremic component, administered fluids and kidney function.","sn.pf_with_support":"Interpret the PaO₂/FiO₂ change alongside trends in FiO₂, PEEP and respiratory support.","sn.po2_not_comparable":"Arterial and non-arterial PO₂ are not the same measurement: no oxygenation trend is plotted.","sn.events_no_causality":"Align recorded treatment and support changes with sample times; several factors may contribute.","so.entry":"Time information missing: points were compared in input order; no hourly change given.","so.resorted":"Points were sorted by timestamp; input IDs were preserved.","mod.renal":"Kidney context (user input)","mod.uag":"Urine anion gap (UAG)","mod.urine":"Urine pH / chloride context","mod.caratio":"Systemic total Ca / ionized Ca ratio","mod.agk":"Potassium-including anion gap (AG_K)","mod.og":"Osmolal gap (OG)","mod.tox":"Exposure context (toxicology teaching card)","mod.salicylate":"Salicylate level and unit","mod.lacgap":"Lactate difference between two methods","err.ica_zero":"Ionized calcium cannot be zero; ratio not calculated (no infinite result is produced).","err.zero_invalid":"This measurement cannot be zero; verify the value. No calculation was made.","m.renal_ctx_user":"Kidney context was entered by the user as clinical information; it was not derived from the blood gas.","m.renal_ctx_none":"Kidney disease was entered as 'none'; this too is not verified by the blood gas.","m.renal_ctx_unknown":"Kidney context unknown: neither CKD nor AKI was assumed, nor was normal kidney function assumed.","m.renal_no_staging":"Blood gas does not give an AKI stage, a CKD stage or a diagnosis of uremia; KDIGO staging is based on creatinine change and urine output.","m.renal_scope_ped":"Child/neonate: the adult CKD bicarbonate example (<18 mmol/L), the adult treatment card or dialysis decisions are not applied; age-specific local evaluation is required.","m.renal_preg_egfr":"Pregnancy: standard eGFR equations are not considered valid in pregnancy; renal function is read together with serum creatinine, the maternal gas and obstetric evaluation.","m.renal_met_acid_candidate":"In this sample, metabolic acidosis is one of the candidate processes. Kidney context may contribute but is not accepted as the sole cause; lactate, ketones, toxins and losses are evaluated separately.","m.renal_hco3_not_alone":"Low HCO₃ alone does not mean metabolic acidosis: it is also seen in the renal response to respiratory alkalosis. It is read together with pH and PCO₂.","m.renal_ag_other_causes":"In kidney disease, too, the non-renal causes of a high AG (lactate, ketones, toxic substance) remain open; the entire AG is not attributed to the kidney.","m.renal_bicarb_evidence":"Acidemia with AKI: the bicarbonate and KRT lesson compares patient populations and outcomes in BICAR-ICU, BICARICU-2 and STARRT-AKI.","m.renal_k_drug_context":"Assess potassium with medications and kidney function. Type 4 RTA may enter the differential; determining the subtype requires investigation beyond the blood gas.","m.krt_under_treatment":"The sample was taken during KRT: pH and HCO₃ also reflect treatment effects. Assess kidney recovery separately using urine output, fluid balance and renal function.","m.renal_info_needed":"Creatinine trajectory, urine output and prior kidney data are not requested on this site; kidney evaluation is done in the clinic with this information.","m.renal_no_treatment":"This card does not generate a diagnosis, stage, dialysis/KRT decision or drug dose.","m.uag_no_zero_fill":"All three of urine Na, K and Cl are required; a missing value is not counted as zero.","m.uag_not_same_sample":"Urine electrolytes are not from the same sample: UAG not calculated.","m.uag_same_unknown":"It has not been verified that the three urine electrolytes come from the same sample: the result is arithmetic only, interpretation is limited.","m.uag_not_ammonium":"UAG is not urine ammonium directly; it can be misleading when non-ammonium anions are excreted.","m.uag_ckd_limit":"In CKD, the standard UAG is a weak surrogate for urine ammonium; direct urine ammonium is preferred where possible.","m.uag_renal_unknown":"Kidney context unknown: UAG was not interpreted assuming normal kidney function.","m.uag_no_subtype":"A positive UAG does not mean definite RTA, and a negative UAG does not mean definite diarrhea; no RTA subtype or treatment is inferred.","m.urine_ph_not_rta":"A single urine pH neither establishes nor excludes a diagnosis of RTA; a distal RTA pattern is evaluated during systemic acidosis, with potassium and kidney context. Urine pH is not the amount of net acid excretion.","m.urine_cl_no_class":"Urine chloride is read together with blood pressure, volume and diuretic history. The <20 / >20 mmol/L groups in the source are described in the lesson; the site does not assign a class automatically.","m.urine_diuretic_limit":"Recent diuretic: limits interpretation of urine electrolytes and chloride.","m.urine_alkali_limit":"Alkali given: limits interpretation of urine pH.","m.urine_infection_limit":"Urinary infection context: limits interpretation of urine pH.","m.urine_ctx_unknown":"At least one of the diuretic, alkali or infection contexts is unknown: not counted as 'none', listed as missing information.","m.urine_no_prescription":"No RTA subtype, fluid, alkali or potassium prescription is generated from urine values.","m.ca_ica_invalid":"Ionized calcium invalid (zero or negative): ratio not calculated.","m.ca_need_pair":"The ratio requires both systemic total Ca and ionized Ca.","m.ca_postfilter":"Post-filter (circuit) ionized calcium is not the patient's systemic iCa: the patient total/iCa ratio was not calculated. The circuit value belongs to monitoring of citrate dosing.","m.ca_site_unknown":"Calcium sampling site unknown: the ratio is not calculated unless both values are verified as systemic.","m.ca_unit_unknown":"Calcium unit not selected: ratio not calculated; the unit is not guessed.","m.ca_unit_mismatch":"Total Ca and iCa are in different units: no silent conversion is made, ratio not calculated.","m.ca_unit_not_mmol":"This version calculates the ratio only with mmol/L input; the mg/dL conversion (molar mass) has not been sourced.","m.ca_not_concurrent":"Total Ca and iCa are not concurrent: a quotient of different samples is not shown as the patient ratio.","m.ca_concurrency_unknown":"Concurrency not verified: the result is arithmetic only; not interpreted in the citrate context.","m.rca_scope_special":"Child, neonate or pregnancy: the RCA source profiles are adult consensus statements and are not carried over to this group; specialist evaluation is required.","m.rca_not_confirmed":"Regional citrate anticoagulation (RCA) not confirmed: the ratio was not interpreted in the citrate context. RCA is not assumed just because KRT is present; a high ratio is not a citrate diagnosis.","m.rca_2026_met":"RCA confirmed and ratio ≥2.5: in the 2026 Delphi consensus profile, this is a contextual sign that, together with other findings, raises suspicion of citrate accumulation. It is not a diagnosis; the calcium requirement trend, acid–base course and clinical evaluation are needed.","m.rca_2026_not_met":"The ratio is below the ≥2.5 condition of the 2026 profile. This does not exclude citrate accumulation; the trend and clinical context are evaluated rather than a single measurement.","m.rca_2023_boundary":"Ratio exactly 2.5: because the 2023 expert opinion uses the wording '>2.5' (or a trend rising toward it), this value does not meet the condition in that profile; the 2026 profile uses '≥2.5'. The profiles are not merged.","m.rca_ca_need_rising":"Calcium requirement entered as increasing: in the sources this is a finding evaluated together with accumulation; alone it is not a diagnosis.","m.rca_trend_unknown":"Calcium requirement trend unknown: a single ratio does not replace the trend.","m.rca_alkalemia_ddx":"Alkalemia during RCA: the alkali load from citrate metabolism and citrate accumulation are different problems. Alkalemia alone is not evidence of accumulation.","m.ca_ratio_not_dx":"The ratio is not a definitive diagnosis of citrate toxicity. No citrate/calcium flow, target or check timing is recommended; albumin-corrected calcium is not used in place of this ratio.","m.agk_k_missing":"Ethylene glycol / toxic alcohol context: the EXTRIP ethylene glycol definition uses the potassium-including AG; K was not entered, AG_K not calculated (K is not counted as zero).","m.agk_definition":"AG_K = Na + K − Cl − HCO₃: the definition in the EXTRIP ethylene glycol document. The EXTRIP methanol document, by contrast, uses the potassium-free AG (Na − Cl − HCO₃).","m.agk_not_interchangeable":"Potassium-including, potassium-free and albumin-corrected AG are separate formulas; the value of one is not compared against the threshold table of another. EXTRIP thresholds are not applied automatically to the patient on this site.","m.og_two_nitrogen":"BUN and urea were both entered: they may be two different presentations of the same analyte and the inconsistency was not resolved. OG is not calculated until a single nitrogen analyte is selected.","m.og_not_concurrent":"Measured osmolality and components are not concurrent: OG not calculated.","m.og_ethanol_unknown":"Ethanol not measured or unknown: not assumed to be 0; OG not calculated while the ethanol contribution is unknown.","m.og_no_zero_fill":"A missing component is not filled with zero; all components and units are required.","m.og_concurrency_unknown":"It has not been verified that the components were taken at the same time as the measured osmolality: the result is arithmetic, interpretation is limited.","m.og_ethanol_zero":"Ethanol measured as 0: ethanol contribution is 0 (in both profiles). In this case, the −0.35 constant of the empirical regression is not applied as a negative contribution.","m.og_profile_needed":"Ethanol positive and no laboratory profile selected: the ideal (÷4.6) and empirical Purssell (÷3.7 − 0.35) profiles are shown separately. No definitive corrected OG is given; select the profile according to your own laboratory.","m.og_profile_ideal":"Selected profile: ideal ethanol contribution (ethanol mg/dL ÷ 4.6).","m.og_profile_purssell":"Selected profile: Purssell empirical regression (ethanol mg/dL ÷ 3.7 − 0.35).","m.og_purssell_negative":"At very low ethanol, the empirical regression gives a negative contribution: this is a limit of the model, not a physical reality.","m.og_negative":"OG negative: not rounded to zero. Check the measurement, unit and formula profile; a negative value does not exclude poisoning.","m.og_suspicion_not_excluded":"Exposure suspected: whatever the OG value, toxic alcohol is not excluded (with delayed presentation the OG may have fallen). Specific analysis and clinical evaluation are required.","m.og_scope_special":"Child, neonate or pregnancy: OG source studies are in adult populations; arithmetic only is shown.","m.og_no_normal":"No universal OG normal range is defined in this package: no 'normal', 'safe' or 'excluded' label is given.","m.og_not_exclude":"OG alone neither excludes nor proves toxic alcohol; it does not answer the same question as the AG.","m.sal_unit_needed":"Salicylate unit not selected: a value without a unit is not converted and is not compared with any source value.","m.sal_units_shown":"Units are shown separately: if a mg/L value is mistaken for mg/dL, there is a tenfold error (1000 mg/L = 100 mg/dL).","m.sal_acidemia_context":"Acidemia together with a salicylate level: a fall in systemic pH matters for tissue distribution; time-sensitive clinical/toxicology evaluation is required.","m.sal_normal_ph_not_normal":"Low PCO₂ and low HCO₃ together may suggest respiratory alkalosis and metabolic acidosis. Their opposing effects may keep pH within the reference range; pH alone therefore does not establish a normal blood gas.","m.sal_level_not_alone":"The level is read together with acute/chronic exposure, serial measurements, pH and clinical course. Chronic toxicity may be significant even at low levels.","m.sal_no_threshold_class":"The EXTRIP recommendations and their strength are provided in the corresponding sources; this card does not automatically place the patient's level into a threshold class and does not generate a dialysis or alkali treatment decision.","m.lacgap_method_note":"Difference between two concurrent methods: when the method is known, it may be a clue to analytical interference (e.g. ethylene glycol metabolites); check the analyzer documentation.","m.lacgap_not_concurrent":"Samples are not concurrent: the difference may also include biological change; it is not called an analytical interference gap.","m.lacgap_concurrency_unknown":"Concurrency not verified: arithmetic only; it is not definitively called an analytical interference gap.","m.lacgap_no_threshold":"There is no universal difference threshold, and not every method is affected in the same way. The difference is not a diagnosis of ethylene glycol or any other substance.","m.tox_no_delay":"Exposure suspicion entered: clinical and toxicology (poison center) evaluation does not wait for completion of this form or for laboratory confirmation. Missing fields only disable the calculations on this page.","m.tox_worsening_urgent":"Suspected exposure together with clinical deterioration: time-sensitive emergency/toxicology evaluation is required. The site does not generate treatment, antidote or dialysis decisions.","m.tox_unknown_not_negative":"Exposure information 'unknown': this does not mean there was no exposure; no substance name is assigned.","m.tox_no_reported":"Exposure entered as 'none'; the blood gas does not verify this.","m.tox_methanol_ag_def":"Methanol: the EXTRIP methanol document defines the AG without potassium (Na − Cl − HCO₃). The albumin-corrected AG does not replace it; the thresholds are in the corresponding EXTRIP source and are not applied automatically to the patient.","m.tox_eg_ag_def":"Ethylene glycol: the EXTRIP ethylene glycol document uses the potassium-including AG (Na + K − Cl − HCO₃), and the gap-based recommendations carry a condition of evidence of exposure. The thresholds are in the corresponding EXTRIP source and are not applied automatically to the patient.","m.tox_alcohol_unspecified":"Type of toxic alcohol uncertain: methanol and ethylene glycol have different AG definitions and different threshold tables; no comparison is made until the type is selected.","m.tox_antidote_unknown":"Antidote (fomepizole/ethanol) status unknown: EXTRIP's antidote-dependent level/OG branches are not selected.","m.tox_antidote_context":"Antidote context entered: interpretation of OG and substance level depends on antidote status; the EXTRIP branches are described in the lesson and are not assigned automatically.","m.tox_salicylate_context":"Salicylate: respiratory alkalosis and high anion gap metabolic acidosis may coexist. Deterioration despite a falling serum level is not reassuring; beware of unit confusion.","m.tox_salicylate_chronic":"Chronic exposure: chronic salicylate toxicity may be significant even at lower levels.","m.tox_metformin_context":"Metformin use and elevated lactate do not by themselves prove causality; contexts such as shock and kidney impairment are evaluated together. The EXTRIP metformin recommendations are in the context of severe poisoning, not for all hyperlactatemia.","m.tox_isopropanol_context":"Isopropanol is metabolized to acetone: ketosis and an osmolal gap may be present without acidosis. Urine ketones, β-hydroxybutyrate and acetone are not the same analyte; ketosis does not mean DKA.","m.tox_bhb_not_measured":"β-hydroxybutyrate not measured: ketone status is not counted as 'none'.","m.tox_co_spo2":"CO exposure: standard pulse oximetry and a normal PaO₂ do not exclude CO poisoning; co-oximetry, exposure history and clinical status are needed together. The existing CaO₂ disabling policy does not change.","m.tox_coox_needed":"COHb not entered: CO evaluation requires blood co-oximetry.","m.tox_co_preg":"CO exposure in pregnancy requires special evaluation; a single adult value is not carried over to this group.","m.tox_smoke_context":"Smoke inhalation: concomitant poisonings, including cyanide, are evaluated clinically. In one study, lactate >10 mmol/L was found to be sensitive for high blood cyanide; this comes from a specific population and is not a diagnostic or antidote rule on the site.","m.tox_lactate_not_cyanide":"Lactate alone is not a diagnosis of cyanide poisoning; a low value does not exclude cyanide either.","m.tox_pg_context":"Infusions containing propylene glycol (drug formulation) may create solvent exposure; exposure is not confirmed from the drug name alone without checking the formulation.","m.oa_dlactate":"Short bowel context: D-lactic acidosis is not visible on routine L-lactate measurement; specific analysis may be considered. This is not a diagnosis.","m.oa_oxoproline":"5-oxoproline (pyroglutamic acid) is a rare cause in the appropriate drug/malnutrition context and requires specific analysis; no automatic diagnosis follows from a drug name.","m.tox_other":"Other exposure: the substance name and timing belong to the clinical evaluation; no substance or dose is inferred from the blood gas.","m.tox_scope_special":"Child, neonate or pregnancy: no automatic evaluation or treatment scheme is derived from adult studies; the existing scope gates apply.","m.tox_no_treatment":"This card does not generate a substance diagnosis, antidote, hyperbaric oxygen, dialysis/EXTRIP decision, dose or discharge recommendation. The EXTRIP recommendations can be consulted in the sources; they are not applied automatically to the patient.","sn.ph_same_components_changed":"pH did not change but PCO₂ and/or HCO₃ changed: this cannot be called 'no change'; the components are read separately. A single pH curve hides this change.","sn.salicylate_fall_not_recovery":"Salicylate level fell: this alone does not mean improvement or that toxicity is over; pH and clinical course are evaluated separately.","sn.salicylate_fall_worsening":"Clinical deterioration was entered at the second point while the level was falling: a falling level is not reassuring; time-sensitive clinical/toxicology evaluation is needed.","sn.salicylate_fall_ph_down":"pH fell while the level was falling: systemic acidemia matters for tissue distribution; the level curve is not read on its own.","sn.krt_event_not_recovery":"There is a KRT event in this interval: the change occurred under treatment. Renal recovery, adequate dialysis dose or a decision to stop KRT is not inferred.","sv.age_missing":"age group not selected (this point was not interpreted; acid–base difference is raw arithmetic only)","sv.sample_out":"sample is outside the scope of this evaluation (acid–base difference is raw arithmetic only)","sw.events_unplaced":"Some events were not placed in any interval (time missing, outside the interval, or the selected points are not consecutive). An event is not assigned to an interval by guesswork.","so.identity_mismatch":"The case labels of the points do not match: no common series was built. Verify the labels."};
